{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Union\nclass MaxDifferenceFunction:\n    @staticmethod\n    def max_difference(pairs: List[Union[Tuple[float, float], Pair]]) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the maximum absolute difference from a list of pairs.\n        Raises ValueError if the input list is empty.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not pairs:\n            raise ValueError(\"pairs must contain at least one pair\")\n\n        max_val_found = float('-inf')\n\n        for item in pairs:\n            if isinstance(item, Pair):\n                current_diff = item.abs_diff()\n            else: # Assumed to be Tuple[float, float] based on type hint\n                current_diff = abs(item[0] - item[1])\n\n            if current_diff > max_val_found:\n                max_val_found = current_diff\n        \n        return max_val_found\ndef max_difference(pairs: List[Union[Tuple[float, float], Pair]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum absolute difference between available pairs in a list of 2-element numeric tuples or Pair instances, raising ValueError on empty input.\n    Example: `max_difference([(3, 5), (1, 7), (10, 3), (1, 2)]) == 7`\n    \"\"\"\n    return MaxDifferenceFunction.max_difference(pairs)"}
