{"task_id": "Mbpp/566", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\ndef _validate_non_negative_integer(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates that the input n is a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(n, int) and n >= 0\ndef _extract_digits(n: int) -> list[Digit]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts decimal digits from a non-negative integer into a list of Digit objects.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return [Digit(value=0, position=0)]\n\n    digits_list = []\n    # Convert to string to iterate, then reverse to assign positions from least-significant (0-based)\n    str_n = str(n)\n    for i, char_digit in enumerate(reversed(str_n)):\n        digits_list.append(Digit(value=int(char_digit), position=i))\n    return digits_list\ndef sum_digits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the digits of a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n    if not _validate_non_negative_integer(n):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    digits = _extract_digits(n)\n    total_sum = sum(digit.value for digit in digits)\n    return SumResult(value=total_sum).value"}
