{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef largest_subset(nums: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset of numbers where every pair is divisible.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n\n    sorted_nums = sorted(nums)\n    return _compute_lis_divisible(sorted_nums)\ndef _compute_lis_divisible(sorted_nums: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the length of the longest divisible chain in a sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(sorted_nums)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    dp = [1] * n\n    max_len = 1\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        val_i = sorted_nums[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            val_j = sorted_nums[j]\n\n            is_divisible_pair = False\n            if val_j == 0:\n                # If val_j is 0, any pair (0, X) is divisible because X divides 0 (0 % X == 0).\n                # (0,0) is divisible because 0 % 0 == 0.\n                is_divisible_pair = True\n            elif val_i == 0: # val_j is not 0, val_i is 0\n                # Any pair (X != 0, 0) is divisible because X divides 0 (0 % X == 0).\n                is_divisible_pair = True\n            else: # Both val_j and val_i are non-zero\n                # Check if val_j divides val_i (val_i % val_j == 0)\n                # or if val_i divides val_j (val_j % val_i == 0)\n                if val_i % val_j == 0 or val_j % val_i == 0:\n                    is_divisible_pair = True\n            \n            if is_divisible_pair:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], 1 + dp[j])\n        max_len = max(max_len, dp[i])\n            \n    return max_len"}
