{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return a new list containing elements of input_list rotated to the right by k positions.\n    Handles empty lists, k=0, and k >= n by using k modulo n.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    effective_k = k % n\n    \n    # The split point determines where the list is divided for rotation.\n    # For a right rotation of 'effective_k' items, the last 'effective_k' items\n    # move to the front, and the first 'n - effective_k' items move to the back.\n    split_point = n - effective_k\n    \n    return input_list[split_point:] + input_list[:split_point]"}
